The viable route is Track B, based on the paper’s native absorbing-edge definition (Section 3, immediately before Lemma 3.2), not the tempting planted almost-perfect matching. I’m implementing a \(3\)-partite \(3\)-graph over \(\mathbb F_2^d\) whose legal co-degree is exact, and asking for one \(S\)-absorbing edge. Generic GF(2) elimination produces a witness in polynomial time and will be reported as the successful reference algorithm; the compact route is the shared XOR invariant through three coordinate changes.
