The first full self-test exposed a performance bug in the test harness path, not the mathematics: each random candidate was recomputing the same row reduction and repeatedly decoding the same binary data. I’m caching those immutable exact structures so the required 200,000 structure-aware trials measure verification rather than setup overhead.
