codex
I found and removed a genuine planting signature before freezing the module: the planted absorber always used the zero syndrome while decoy edges used every target syndrome. The revised construction makes the planted syndrome depend symmetrically on the instance—specifically, on the syndrome difference of the two \(V_1\) vertices—and embeds that value as a global XOR invariant of the target set. The witness is still obtained by three XOR identities, but it is no longer “the zero-syndrome edge.” I’ll rerun density and all attacks after this change.
