codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 3 \(S\)-absorbing-edge definition ([arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.04838)).

Local verification passes all G1–G9(c) gates:

- 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses succeeded.
- Four attacks scored 0/8 each.
- Gaussian reference algorithm solved 8/8 at 18,408 counted operations.
- 100/100 relabelling checks passed.
- 20/20 shipping instances had distinct canonical keys.
- Answer size: 250 characters; intended route: 240 XORs.

Files:

- [gen_1608_04838.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/gen_1608_04838.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.04838/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not submission-ready: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every oracle call, so no scored hardening or G9 attempt exists. The transcripts preserve those genuine harness failures; none were misreported as model failures. Restore the OpenRouter quota and rerun `harden.py` to complete the required external evidence.
